=== ISSUE ===
Title: create_simul, join_simul, withdraw_from_simul and get_thread call endpoints that don't exist (404)

The Lichess API spec (https://github.com/lichess-org/api/blob/906d1a6e93ca1ba4b65c9decb3077f2431c6d55a/doc/specs/lichess-api.yaml) has only `GET /api/simul` for simuls, and no endpoint for reading an inbox thread (only `POST /inbox/{username}` for sending).

Live, without a token:
- POST /api/simul/new, /api/simul/{id}/join, /api/simul/{id}/withdraw: 404
- GET /api/inbox/{user}: 404
- The site-root versions are website routes, not API endpoints; GET /inbox/{user} redirects (303) to the login page.

The test comments say these were kept for usability and backward compatibility, but every call fails.

